  ],
  "slug": "conformational-protein-8241",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend confidence scoring and epitope retrieval beyond protein-protein contacts to nucleic acid and ligand interactions.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is learned or geometric scoring that ranks candidates for downstream use. EpiRank retrieves surface patches as epitope candidates from single-chain geometry, reporting a 1.57x lift over random under leakage controls, while the ipSAE extension adds directional PAE scoring to AF3 and Boltz-2 cofolding complexes spanning protein, nucleic acid, ligand and ion interactions. RPI-Zero applies sequence-only zero-shot prediction to protein-RNA interactions, evaluated on a leakage-free CLIP benchmark of 2.1M examples across 209 proteins, where it outperforms five methods. What is new is confidence scoring and benchmarking extended beyond protein-protein contacts, with leakage handled explicitly. A separate AlphaFold analysis finds that most of 237,922 binding pockets across 12,255 proteins are holo-like, a bias relevant to pocket detection and docking.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
